CDC-15-CO-01 Tries to use things the right way, like a phone, cup, or book
CDC-15-MP-02 Uses fingers to feed herself some food
CDC-18-SE-01 Moves away from you, but looks to make sure you are close by
CDC-18-SE-03 Puts hands out for you to wash them
CDC-18-SE-04 Looks at a few pages in a book with you
CDC-18-LC-01 Tries to say three or more words besides “mama” or “dada”
CDC-18-LC-02 Follows one-step directions without any gestures, like giving you the toy when you say, “Give it to me.”
CDC-18-CO-01 Copies you doing chores, like sweeping with a broom
CDC-18-MP-01 Walks without holding on to anyone or anything
CDC-18-MP-03 Drinks from a cup without a lid and may spill sometimes
CDC-18-MP-04 Feeds himself with his fingers
CDC-18-MP-05 Tries to use a spoon
CDC-18-MP-06 Climbs on and off a couch or chair without help
CDC-24-SE-01 Notices when others are hurt or upset, like pausing or looking sad when someone is crying
CDC-24-SE-02 Looks at your face to see how to react in a new situation
CDC-24-LC-01 Points to things in a book when you ask, like “Where is the bear?”
CDC-24-LC-03 Points to at least two body parts when you ask him to show you
CDC-24-LC-04 Uses more gestures than just waving and pointing, like blowing a kiss or nodding yes
CDC-24-CO-03 Plays with more than one toy at the same time, like putting toy food on a toy plate
CDC-24-MP-02 Runs
CDC-24-MP-03 Walks (not climbs) up a few stairs with or without help
CDC-30-SE-01 Plays next to other children and sometimes plays with them
CDC-30-SE-02 Shows you what she can do by saying, “Look at me!”
CDC-30-SE-03 Follows simple routines when told, like helping to pick up toys when you say, “It’s clean-up time.”
CDC-30-LC-03 Names things in a book when you point and ask, “What is this?”
CDC-30-CO-01 Uses things to pretend, like feeding a block to a doll as if it were food
CDC-30-CO-02 Shows simple problem-solving skills, like standing on a small stool to reach something
CDC-36-SE-01 Calms down within 10 minutes after you leave her, like at a childcare drop off
CDC-36-SE-02 Notices other children and joins them to play
CDC-36-LC-01 Talks with you in conversation using at least two back-and-forth exchanges
CDC-36-LC-02 Asks “who,” “what,” “where,” or “why” questions, like “Where is mommy/daddy?”
CDC-36-LC-03 Says what action is happening in a picture or book when asked, like “running,” “eating,” or “playing”
CDC-36-LC-04 Says first name, when asked
CDC-36-CO-01 Draws a circle, when you show him how
CDC-36-CO-02 Avoids touching hot objects, like a stove, when you warn her
CDC-48-SE-02 Asks to go play with children if none are around, like “Can I play with Alex?”
CDC-48-SE-04 Avoids danger, like not jumping from tall heights at the playground
CDC-48-SE-05 Likes to be a “helper”
CDC-48-SE-06 Changes behavior based on where she is (place of worship, library, playground)
CDC-48-LC-04 Answers simple questions like “What is a coat for?” or “What is a crayon for?”
CDC-48-CO-02 Tells what comes next in a well-known story
CDC-48-CO-03 Draws a person with three or more body parts
CDC-48-MP-01 Catches a large ball most of the time
CDC-48-MP-04 Holds crayon or pencil between fingers and thumb (not a fist)

apply patch
